    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm also concerned about the potential for sudden, unpredictable changes in friction performance if the temperature spikes too quickly—kind of like if the system just starts acting up or behaving erratically due to thermal instability. How do these two materials handle those sudden thermal shocks/spikes compared to each other?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Carbon-ceramic pads generally handle sudden thermal shocks better due to their faster thermal conductivity, which enables quicker temperature stabilization without as much shear-induced stress or friction fluctuation. Semi-metallic pads, on the other hand, can exhibit more erratic friction performance when encountering abrupt temperature changes, because their slower heating and cooling rates can lead to inconsistent friction levels and potential brake fade in high-stress scenarios.",
      "source": "target",
