      "content": "Yeah, that inconsistent friction is a big worry for the testing phase. We've seen some instances in the simulation where the braking force just seems to drop off or fluctuate for no apparent reason right when the heat peaks, making the whole system feel like it's being sabotaged or playing tricks on the driver. From a material science perspective, is there any specific chemical or structural reason why semi-metallic pads would exhibit that kind of \"mischievous\" or unpredictable behavior during a spike?",
