      "content": "During thermal spikes, semi-metallic pads can experience changes in their composite structure, such as expansion of metallic components and worsening of the ceramic matrix interaction due to poor thermal conductance. The higher heat capacity of metals within these pads may also cause uneven thermal expansion, leading to inconsistencies in the friction coefficient and the resultant fluctuating braking force. Additionally, the silicon carbide particles and metal fibers can separate under extreme heat, altering the pad's effective frictional properties. These changes contribute to the unpredictable performance behavior observed during sudden heat spikes.",
